Now I have a good understanding of the change. The `handle_trace` function was previously using `read_events` which reads ALL events - on large event histories (288K+), this was timing out. The fix introduces a `read_trace_events` function that scans backwards in expanding chunks (starting from 20K, doubling up to 200K) from the tail of the event store, since run events are temporally contiguous near the end. This avoids reading the entire event history.

